WEBVTT

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:19.730
What the hell is this?

00:00:19.730 --> 00:00:22.690
What's going on here?

00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:27.320
This didn't happen in <i>No Longer Human</i> .

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:28.400
Which means...

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:38.230
He was right.

00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:40.070
You really came.

00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:41.110
Dazai!

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:44.230
Dazai- <i>kun</i> --

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:45.570
The name's Oba.

00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:52.940
Oba Yozo.

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:52.940
"I have led a life filled with shame."

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:26.150
I see.

00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:32.730
So you believe that Akutagawa Ryunosuke
was always possessed by a Taint.

00:02:32.730 --> 00:02:35.230
It's just a hypothesis.

00:02:35.230 --> 00:02:41.280
But if it were true, it would explain
his later denial of his early works.

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:46.860
The author of <i>Rashomon</i> and <i>Spider's Thread</i>
is Akutagawa Ryunosuke.

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:53.860
And it was the Taint who possessed him
that wrote <i>Gears</i> and <i>Kappa</i> .

00:02:53.860 --> 00:02:56.110
But that's impossible.

00:02:56.110 --> 00:02:57.280
Why?

00:02:57.280 --> 00:03:02.190
Taints are collections of negative feelings
towards literature.

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:07.070
They despise the act of creation
and are driven to destroy its works.

00:03:07.070 --> 00:03:09.570
They're the opposite of authors.

00:03:11.150 --> 00:03:16.150
In other words, you're saying
a Taint can't be creative.

00:03:16.150 --> 00:03:20.480
But then how do you explain this?

00:03:22.110 --> 00:03:24.600
"Episode 9"

00:03:23.860 --> 00:03:26.610
"Am I truly happy?"

00:03:28.030 --> 00:03:30.030
Okay, here we go.

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:31.860
Get ready!

00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:47.730
I don't know what it means to be human.

00:03:49.820 --> 00:03:54.530
For instance, I don't understand hunger.

00:03:54.530 --> 00:03:58.900
Everyone says they eat because they get hungry.

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:04.690
But I've never eaten because I was hungry.

00:04:04.690 --> 00:04:09.690
Supposedly, it's normal to get angry
when something unpleasant happens.

00:04:09.690 --> 00:04:16.360
But the face of an angry human seemed
scarier to me than a lion or a dragon.

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:19.980
I could never see myself being that way.

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:24.860
When I think of that frightening form
as a necessary part of being human,

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:27.230
I feel despair.

00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:29.780
"Lion Mane"

00:04:30.820 --> 00:04:35.440
Being given a gift was
the greatest pain imaginable.

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:41.030
Because I couldn't think of a thing I wanted.

00:04:48.730 --> 00:04:57.570
But I couldn't bring myself
to have said I didn't want it.

00:04:57.570 --> 00:04:58.570
"I put up a front of carefree innocence, and gradually,"

00:04:58.570 --> 00:05:03.320
"I became a clown, a weirdo."

00:04:58.570 --> 00:05:03.320
I didn't understand humanity. They scared me.

00:05:03.320 --> 00:05:05.860
"Gradually, that became all I was."

00:05:03.320 --> 00:05:06.320
To keep people from finding that out,

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:10.150
I had no choice but to play the fool.

00:05:10.150 --> 00:05:15.230
I thought that if I could make
them laugh, no matter how,

00:05:15.230 --> 00:05:18.320
I could pretend to be human.

00:05:18.320 --> 00:05:21.820
I played the fool at school, too.

00:05:28.690 --> 00:05:30.030
Oww!

00:05:31.690 --> 00:05:34.860
Terrifyingly enough,

00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:40.320
they all respected me for making them laugh.

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:41.650
But...

00:05:47.900 --> 00:05:50.860
Deliberate. Deliberate.

00:05:54.230 --> 00:05:59.190
I was terrified. Because he'd seen through me.

00:06:01.730 --> 00:06:04.480
My playing the fool didn't work on him.

00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:06.980
He'd seen through me.

00:06:06.980 --> 00:06:11.030
When I thought about it,
I wanted to scream and run away.

00:06:20.190 --> 00:06:21.190
Hey.

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:25.730
I decided to be his friend.

00:06:25.730 --> 00:06:30.650
So that he wouldn't tell
everyone it was just an act.

00:06:30.650 --> 00:06:33.650
Why don't you come over?

00:06:36.360 --> 00:06:38.230
Don't force yourself.

00:06:38.230 --> 00:06:40.820
You're not fooling anybody.

00:06:42.190 --> 00:06:43.530
Aww, what are you--

00:06:43.530 --> 00:06:45.940
You can play the fool,

00:06:45.940 --> 00:06:50.940
but you can never be a human.

00:06:50.940 --> 00:06:54.030
What are you saying?

00:06:54.030 --> 00:07:01.570
You should know... how this story ends.

00:07:12.900 --> 00:07:17.610
The person you are, in a sense, attracts others.

00:07:17.610 --> 00:07:20.610
Women will fall in love with you.

00:07:20.610 --> 00:07:23.820
But it will never heal your heart.

00:07:23.820 --> 00:07:25.500
"The woman died. And I survived."

00:07:23.820 --> 00:07:29.070
You can't ever be human.

00:07:29.070 --> 00:07:33.480
No matter how hard you try.
No matter how you disguise yourself.

00:07:33.480 --> 00:07:35.900
It will all come out in the end.

00:07:44.650 --> 00:07:47.530
And then you'll be branded...

00:07:48.980 --> 00:07:52.900
...as No Longer Human.

00:07:54.070 --> 00:07:56.570
No, I...

00:07:56.570 --> 00:08:00.110
That is the conclusion of this story.

00:08:00.110 --> 00:08:02.570
You'll fail to play the fool.

00:08:02.570 --> 00:08:06.860
Fail to be one of the humans.

00:08:06.860 --> 00:08:09.780
It hurts to keep acting, doesn't it?

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:14.480
It's nothing but terror, living next
to humans you don't understand.

00:08:14.480 --> 00:08:17.820
There's no need for you to endure it.

00:08:18.860 --> 00:08:20.320
I...

00:08:20.320 --> 00:08:22.820
Your screams will remain unheard.

00:08:22.820 --> 00:08:29.820
If you're going to suffer,
and suffer, and suffer...

00:08:29.820 --> 00:08:32.610
...before reaching a tragic end,

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:34.980
then why don't you just do whatever you want?

00:08:38.900 --> 00:08:41.730
I just don't understand.

00:08:41.730 --> 00:08:44.190
I don't understand humans.

00:08:44.190 --> 00:08:48.980
I tried to fit in anyway. As a clown.

00:08:48.980 --> 00:08:51.900
But it's a waste of time. All of it.

00:08:51.900 --> 00:08:53.940
Every last bit.

00:08:53.940 --> 00:08:59.150
I'm No Longer Human.

00:08:59.150 --> 00:09:00.780
You...

00:09:00.780 --> 00:09:03.530
I'm scared of what I don't understand.

00:09:03.530 --> 00:09:08.650
And when something scares you,
you have to get rid of it, right?

00:09:08.650 --> 00:09:12.030
I don't want to be the hero of a tragedy.

00:09:12.030 --> 00:09:13.780
I'm going to change.

00:09:16.650 --> 00:09:21.110
If I can't be human...

00:09:21.110 --> 00:09:23.360
...I'll no longer try.

00:09:23.360 --> 00:09:27.780
You're a lot more boring now, Dazai!

00:09:33.650 --> 00:09:35.730
I understand now.

00:09:35.730 --> 00:09:39.150
You're not the Dazai we know.

00:09:39.150 --> 00:09:43.230
We'll have to wake you up.

00:09:43.230 --> 00:09:44.900
I see.

00:09:44.900 --> 00:09:48.030
So you're going to make me suffer too, huh?

00:09:48.030 --> 00:09:51.320
I'll just have to kill you.

00:10:02.230 --> 00:10:04.690
Why are you so desperate?

00:10:04.690 --> 00:10:06.030
Why?

00:10:06.030 --> 00:10:09.820
Because I want to save my friend.

00:10:09.820 --> 00:10:12.940
That's what makes you human, isn't it?

00:10:12.940 --> 00:10:14.730
Not that I'd understand.

00:10:16.650 --> 00:10:17.650
Ango!

00:10:18.530 --> 00:10:19.940
Oda Saku!

00:10:20.780 --> 00:10:22.230
Dazai!

00:10:25.190 --> 00:10:26.980
What's this?

00:10:26.980 --> 00:10:29.280
The Taint is growing stronger!

00:10:29.280 --> 00:10:30.650
What's going on?

00:10:31.980 --> 00:10:33.980
It's so loud.

00:10:33.980 --> 00:10:37.070
It seems things aren't going well.

00:10:38.530 --> 00:10:44.150
Why did you want to taint
Dazai- <i>kun</i> 's book so badly?

00:10:44.150 --> 00:10:45.820
It wasn't my will.

00:10:45.820 --> 00:10:49.280
So it was the will of the Taint?

00:10:49.280 --> 00:10:55.530
You have two minds inside
your body now, essentially.

00:10:55.530 --> 00:10:58.860
That would explain it.

00:10:58.860 --> 00:11:01.530
Release me, please.

00:11:01.530 --> 00:11:03.360
I can't.

00:11:05.320 --> 00:11:06.940
I have to go.

00:11:12.030 --> 00:11:16.780
Are you Akutagawa Ryunosuke? Or...

00:11:16.780 --> 00:11:18.570
It doesn't matter which.

00:11:18.570 --> 00:11:22.570
I just want to save Dazai- <i>kun</i> .

00:11:36.280 --> 00:11:38.190
What are you doing?

00:11:38.190 --> 00:11:41.320
I'm interested in you now.

00:11:41.320 --> 00:11:44.400
An author who's half Taint.

00:11:44.400 --> 00:11:46.940
That's not something you see every day.

00:11:50.820 --> 00:11:52.070
True.

00:11:57.940 --> 00:11:59.900
I hope it works.

00:12:01.900 --> 00:12:03.780
Pray for me.

00:12:17.940 --> 00:12:19.480
What was that sound?

00:12:19.480 --> 00:12:20.480
Shusei?

00:12:22.480 --> 00:12:25.320
Is that book tainted?

00:12:25.320 --> 00:12:28.030
His own suggestion.

00:12:28.030 --> 00:12:34.320
If he was a Taint, he said, he could use this method.

00:12:30.860 --> 00:12:33.940
"Dazai Osamu: The Novel" "Dan Kazuo"

00:12:39.940 --> 00:12:41.690
Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> !

00:12:41.690 --> 00:12:45.940
Why?

00:12:47.360 --> 00:12:49.190
"Akutagawa Ryunosuke Found Dead By Suicide in
Home, Took Drugs and Left 4 Wills"

00:12:49.320 --> 00:12:50.900
Sensei!

00:12:50.900 --> 00:12:54.440
Why didn't you give me the Akutagawa Prize?

00:12:54.440 --> 00:12:57.530
You said it was a good story!

00:12:57.530 --> 00:12:59.900
Are you betraying me?

00:13:03.940 --> 00:13:05.780
Damn it!

00:13:05.780 --> 00:13:08.070
Why?

00:13:08.070 --> 00:13:11.980
There are two methods by which
we authors may be summoned.

00:13:11.980 --> 00:13:14.820
One, to be called by the stones.

00:13:14.820 --> 00:13:16.780
The other...

00:13:16.780 --> 00:13:19.980
...to be rescued from tainted books.

00:13:24.820 --> 00:13:25.820
Ango!

00:13:28.900 --> 00:13:34.110
Why does everyone look so happy all the time?

00:13:34.110 --> 00:13:36.780
Tell me. Why?

00:13:46.650 --> 00:13:50.320
Betraying each other. Deceiving each other.

00:13:50.320 --> 00:13:52.780
And still you laugh with each other.

00:13:55.480 --> 00:13:57.820
I don't understand it.

00:14:00.320 --> 00:14:03.190
I don't understand.

00:14:03.190 --> 00:14:04.940
Then...

00:14:04.940 --> 00:14:07.150
...think!

00:14:07.150 --> 00:14:10.280
If you don't understand, then think!

00:14:12.610 --> 00:14:16.150
Keep thinking! Stop running!

00:14:24.230 --> 00:14:25.940
Dazai- <i>kun</i> .

00:14:27.550 --> 00:14:30.930
"Dazai Osamu: The Novel" "Dan Kazuo"

00:14:28.400 --> 00:14:31.730
An author's books contain his soul.

00:14:31.730 --> 00:14:37.900
By manifesting that soul and tainting it,
the Taints attempt to destroy the books.

00:14:37.900 --> 00:14:44.400
But driving away the Taint allows you
to summon the author's soul.

00:14:44.400 --> 00:14:47.440
So this Taint is...

00:14:49.190 --> 00:14:52.940
It's all an attempt to reincarnate "him."

00:14:54.530 --> 00:14:57.030
It's not a good idea to drink too much.

00:14:57.030 --> 00:14:59.280
Shut up!

00:14:59.280 --> 00:15:01.570
I have to drink.

00:15:06.190 --> 00:15:10.650
There's nothing attractive
about Dazai- <i>kun</i> right now.

00:15:10.650 --> 00:15:12.900
He's just a bratty little kid.

00:15:21.030 --> 00:15:22.360
You need to understand...

00:15:22.360 --> 00:15:26.530
It wasn't a boring person like that
that we were interested in!

00:15:26.530 --> 00:15:29.480
We... and him!

00:15:30.280 --> 00:15:33.820
I can't have you dying of drink.

00:15:33.820 --> 00:15:37.360
I told you. You're a genius.

00:15:37.360 --> 00:15:39.280
I want you to write more.

00:15:44.730 --> 00:15:49.320
If anyone can go inside
<i>No Longer Human</i> , it's time.

00:15:49.320 --> 00:15:55.400
The author of <i>Dazai Osamu: The Novel</i> ,
and the last of the Reprobates.

00:16:04.150 --> 00:16:05.320
What?

00:16:07.480 --> 00:16:09.360
Hey.

00:16:09.360 --> 00:16:10.110
It's been a while.

00:16:10.110 --> 00:16:12.940
"Dan Kazuo"

00:16:13.400 --> 00:16:15.110
Dan- <i>kun</i> !

00:16:15.110 --> 00:16:16.610
What are you doing here?

00:16:16.610 --> 00:16:19.230
I'll tell you.

00:16:19.230 --> 00:16:20.900
For now...

00:16:21.940 --> 00:16:24.730
What are you?

00:16:24.730 --> 00:16:27.360
That's my line.

00:16:27.360 --> 00:16:30.940
You look pathetic, Dazai.

00:16:30.940 --> 00:16:33.940
I don't know you!

00:16:36.730 --> 00:16:41.610
Yes, the hero of this story
ends his life in tragedy.

00:16:41.610 --> 00:16:42.820
But you know...

00:16:42.820 --> 00:16:44.320
Stay away!

00:16:45.820 --> 00:16:52.110
The way you tried to be a human
until the very end was beautiful.

00:16:52.110 --> 00:16:53.860
Shut up!

00:16:53.860 --> 00:16:57.650
You really are a genius, Dazai.

00:16:57.650 --> 00:17:00.110
Because you can write a story like this.

00:17:00.110 --> 00:17:02.280
Shut up!

00:17:05.860 --> 00:17:12.280
For Yozo, the protagonist,
humanity was a bright light that burnt him.

00:17:12.280 --> 00:17:16.650
Even as he knew it would burn him,
he still longed for it.

00:17:19.070 --> 00:17:21.570
So don't give up on your longing!

00:17:21.570 --> 00:17:24.650
Reach out for the light that burns you!

00:17:24.650 --> 00:17:27.480
Don't hide in the shadows!

00:17:35.980 --> 00:17:38.190
I... Oww!

00:17:38.190 --> 00:17:40.690
You're finally back to sanity?

00:17:40.690 --> 00:17:43.730
That was a pain.

00:17:43.730 --> 00:17:46.030
Oda Saku! Ango!

00:17:47.980 --> 00:17:48.980
Dan?!

00:17:48.980 --> 00:17:49.730
Yo.

00:17:49.730 --> 00:17:53.070
What are you doing here?
It's been forever.

00:17:53.070 --> 00:17:57.030
We can talk about that later.

00:17:57.030 --> 00:18:01.400
Wow, he got all big.

00:18:01.400 --> 00:18:04.530
Sorry, but I'm not that excited about it now.

00:18:07.780 --> 00:18:10.530
Let's do it, guys.

00:18:10.530 --> 00:18:14.480
Let's show them what our gang
of Reprobates can do.

00:18:31.900 --> 00:18:32.820
Now!

00:18:32.820 --> 00:18:33.860
Go!

00:18:42.280 --> 00:18:43.320
Dazai!

00:18:46.280 --> 00:18:47.480
Come on!

00:18:54.940 --> 00:18:58.360
Here we go!

00:19:21.320 --> 00:19:23.360
I'm tired.

00:19:23.360 --> 00:19:27.230
Now the story will be restored, huh?

00:19:27.230 --> 00:19:32.980
Now it's just up to the
protagonist to finish the story.

00:19:32.980 --> 00:19:35.070
Are you okay now?

00:19:36.820 --> 00:19:37.940
Yeah.

00:19:37.940 --> 00:19:39.650
I won't run anymore.

00:19:40.610 --> 00:19:45.690
Even if it's rough, I'll keep playing the fool.

00:19:53.570 --> 00:19:57.150
Okay, everybody. See you later.

00:19:57.150 --> 00:20:01.940
I need to go live a life full of shame.

00:20:19.570 --> 00:20:20.780
Dazai- <i>kun</i> !

00:20:22.690 --> 00:20:24.190
Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> !

00:20:28.400 --> 00:20:32.400
It's thanks to him that
Dan Kazuo was able to revive.

00:20:34.030 --> 00:20:36.320
I don't really want to say it, but...

00:20:38.190 --> 00:20:40.070
He tried hard, I think.

00:20:41.530 --> 00:20:42.900
He's...

00:20:44.070 --> 00:20:46.070
Dazai- <i>kun</i> .

00:20:46.070 --> 00:20:48.570
I'm sorry. I...

00:20:48.570 --> 00:20:50.070
It's fine.

00:20:50.070 --> 00:20:53.320
I'm a loser.

00:20:53.320 --> 00:20:57.070
It's natural to be told so.

00:20:57.070 --> 00:21:01.610
But I'm still going to try my best to be normal.

00:21:03.360 --> 00:21:05.360
So watch me, okay?

00:21:08.780 --> 00:21:10.110
Okay.

00:21:14.730 --> 00:21:18.480
What? What is this?

00:21:18.480 --> 00:21:20.440
What's happening?

00:21:25.480 --> 00:21:28.610
We're almost to the repair room--

00:21:28.610 --> 00:21:30.190
Get away from him.

00:21:32.150 --> 00:21:33.860
Who are you?

00:21:33.860 --> 00:21:35.940
Didn't you hear me?

00:21:35.940 --> 00:21:38.480
I said get away.

00:21:38.480 --> 00:21:40.400
What are you talking about?

00:21:40.400 --> 00:21:42.190
Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> is...

00:21:52.820 --> 00:21:55.900
"No Longer Human"

00:23:26.480 --> 00:23:28.190
"Literary Gourmet"!

00:23:28.190 --> 00:23:30.650
" <i>Mizu Yokan</i> and Summer Memories"!

00:23:30.650 --> 00:23:33.440
I only invited Dazai, but...

00:23:33.440 --> 00:23:35.110
We're here for free food!

00:23:35.110 --> 00:23:39.480
I recommend the ice cream soda here!
You guys get it!

00:23:39.480 --> 00:23:40.820
I want curry!

00:23:40.820 --> 00:23:42.190
I want a rice omelet!

00:23:42.190 --> 00:23:43.530
Is there no udon?

00:23:43.530 --> 00:23:44.360
Hey!

00:23:44.360 --> 00:23:47.110
You want an ice cream soda, right?

00:23:47.110 --> 00:23:50.820
I remember I used to have fun
with my friends like this.

00:23:50.610 --> 00:23:55.870
" <i>Mizu Yokan</i> " "A mildly sweet <i>yokan</i> . Perfect for
summer, it looks mouthwatering and delicious."

00:23:50.820 --> 00:23:55.440
The mild sweetness,
the way it slid down your throat... I remember it all.

00:23:56.570 --> 00:23:57.980
I'll take a <i>mizu yokan</i> --

00:23:57.980 --> 00:23:59.900
Five ice cream sodas!
